ADDENDA <Act No. 21358, Feb. 19, 2026>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to notification of details of measures against retired executives)
The amended provisions of Article 15-3(1) and (2) shall also apply to the executives and employees who committed a violation before enforcement of this Act and then retired or resigned after enforcement of this Act.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning reporting by virtual asset service providers)
A virtual asset service provider who has filed a report under the previous Article 7 (1) at the time this Act enters into force shall file a report in accordance with the amended provisions of Article 7(1) within 3 months from the date this Act enters into force. In such cases, for the purpose of applying Article 7(6), the date on which the report was accepted shall be deemed the date on which the report was accepted under the previous Article 7(1).
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning acceptance of reports regarding representatives, executives, and major shareholders of virtual asset service providers)
Where a person who, as at the time this Act enters into force, is a representative, executive, or major shareholder of a virtual asset service provider that has filed a report under the previous Article 7(1) falls under the amended provisions of Article 7(3)3 or 5 due to a ground that arose before this Act enters into force, the previous provisions shall apply to the acceptance of a report, etc. with respect to such person, notwithstanding those amended provisions, until such representative, executive, or major shareholder is replaced.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning acceptance of reports by virtual asset service providers)
Where a person who, as at the time this Act enters into force, is a virtual asset service provider that has filed a report under the previous Article 7(1) falls under the amended provisions of Article 7(3)3 or 5 due to a ground that arose before this Act enters into force, the previous provisions shall apply to the acceptance of a report, etc. with respect to such person, notwithstanding those amended provisions.
